    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0237" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/10–1244: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stewart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-12T16:00:00-06:00">October 12, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 18—5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–428. In compliance with the Department’s telegraphic instruction no. 402 of
                    September 27, 4 p.m., I talked with President Somoza concerning the boundary
                    situation, and he repeated what he had said to Bonsal and me last June (see
                    despatch no. 2316 of June 12, 1944<anchor n="23" xml:id="d185-f1"/>). He stated
                    that he and Carías were on friendly terms at present and thought that this was a
                    very good time to endeavor to settle question. He said that he would be willing
                    to talk with Carías in Tegucigalpa, but remarked that some “spade work” would
                    have to be done first in persuading him that if Nicaragua would agree to
                    relinquish its claims to the Aguan and the Patuca, the crest of the mountain
                    line west from Cruta would be an advantageous settlement for Honduras. He said
                    that the best solution would be the creation of a Central American Union.</p>
                <p>I expect to pursue the matter further.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
